HDD / SSD

throughput: the amount of data transferred per second. 
----> measured in mb/s 
---> if your disk has 205mb/s throughput means it can transfer 250 mb/s of data per second 

IOPS: Input Output operation per Second
---> it measures how many read or write operations a storage system can handle per second.
---> if disk offers 3000iops it can perform 3000 read or writes per second.

**Instance Purchasing options:
1. On-demand Instance ---> AWS On-demand
2. Commited use Discount (CUD) ---> Saving plan in AWS
3. Spot Instance --> Spot instance in AWS
4. Reservation --> Capacity Reservation in AWS
5. Sole Tenant Instance ---> Dedicated host in AWS
6. Sustained Use Discount  --> Automatic
--> discount automatically applied if VM runs a significant portion of the month.
--> No commmitment is required. discount is based on usage time.

